    "perplexity": {
      "description": "1993–2000 is a deluxe box set that collects Monster Magnet’s four major-label albums from that period: Superjudge (1993), Dopes to Infinity (1995), Powertrip (1998), and God Says No (2000). Issued through [PIAS] Recordings, it presents the band’s most commercially visible era in one package, with each album newly reissued across eight LPs.\n\nThe set captures Monster Magnet at their peak blend of stoner rock, hard rock, psychedelia, and heavy metal, when Dave Wyndorf’s group refined a massive, riff-driven sound into something both heavy and strangely spacey. It is significant as a snapshot of the band’s evolution from cult favorites into one of the defining acts of late-’90s heavy rock, and the remastered presentation has been noted for highlighting the power and charisma of these recordings.",
